# M3 — Generic Pursuit And Result Seam

Make pursuit reusable, durable, generic beyond software patches, and independent of any one Session, model, worker, or harness.

## Why this is next

M3 depends on `M1` and `M2` in [`sequence.v1.json`](../program/sequence.v1.json): M1 supplies a bounded System with a protected constitutional and lifecycle identity, and M2 supplies deployment, membership, fencing, and transition truth that a long-lived pursuit can be fenced against. M3 adds the reusable definition layer above that identity — immutable profiles, workflows, skills, harness bindings — and the generic result seam that carries outcomes which are not software patches. It also carries the production mechanism spine (information flow and declassification, receipt checkpoint and offline proof, Agentgres writer/branch effects) that later product and sovereignty claims draw on. The stage's `notes` field records the differential under which direct non-System work may proceed without a verified System binding.

