## In scope

- `M3.1` admit immutable `GoalRunProfile` and `WorkflowTemplate` releases as distinct owners.
- `M3.2` resolve exact component requirements and freeze profile revision/hash, admitted overrides, transitive component set, and resolution receipt into every new GoalRun.
- `M3.3` bind `SkillManifest`, `SkillEntry`, and `ActiveSkillSetSnapshot` without giving instructions executable authority.
- `M3.4` operate the GoalKernel orient-plan-act-observe-verify-correct loop over explicit `GoalGroundingLoop` state.
- `M3.5` bind HarnessProfile/AgentHarnessAdapter resolution and leased `RuntimeToolContract`s without making MCP or a harness runtime truth.
- `M3.6` admit generic `WorkResult` and `OutcomeDelta`, retaining `ImplementationResultPayload` as one profile.
- `M3.7` bind typed lifecycle, cancellation fanout, archive, snapshot, and archive-only replay at each owner's legal mutation boundary.
- `M3.8` preserve negative, invalid, inconclusive, superseded, and challenged outputs.
- Own `production-information-flow-and-declassification`, `production-receipt-checkpoint-and-offline-proof`, and `agentgres-production-readiness-and-branch-effects` as M3 mechanism records; M9 must aggregate their selected-profile evidence before the first sovereign-product claim, and the existing M3 direct-path/exit aggregate must join all three while retaining the direct-path differential.
- Runtime truth/action/final-invoker spine: GoalRun/Kernel, ContextCell/Lease/Handoff, Session/WorkRun, and Invocation/Result/Receipt crossings, so no client, harness, or MCP transport can inject accepted truth.
- Direct/non-System and System lifecycle-state proof across the pulled product surfaces: Work / Goals, Sessions, Studio, Automations, Developer Workspace, Provenance.
- Positive, adversarial, stale-state, substitution, fault, recovery, product/operator-state, compatibility, migration, and retained-evidence obligations for the selected profile of each record.

## Out of scope

- Collective pursuit, OutcomeRoom admission, plurality fan-out, and Campaign structure (M4 and later); acceptance authority over results.
- Ownership of the Work, Automations, and Developer Workspace application journeys themselves — M3 owns only the shared lifecycle projection families those journeys read (M6 owns the workspaces and catalog).
- Enterprise learning, improvement campaigns, and model-supply substitution economics (M8); multi-node continuity and cross-failure-domain reconstruction (M10 and later).
- P0 readiness, independent-party operation, or production claims of any kind.

